.TH SUPIVPN-CONTROLLER 8 "October 2026" "SupiVPN" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
supivpn-controller \- serve SupiVPN login and authorization requests
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B supivpn-controller
.BI \-config " file"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the HTTPS controller and a private Unix agent listener using an already
provisioned PostgreSQL database. Database migrations are a separate operation.
The Debian service uses /etc/supivpn/controller/controller.json and the
supivpn-controller system account.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " file"
Read JSON configuration. The standalone default is /etc/supivpn/controller.json.
.TP
.B \-h
Show command-line help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SUPIVPN_DATABASE_URL
Database connection string for the restricted runtime identity.
Keep it out of command-line arguments and logs. The Debian unit reads it from
/etc/supivpn/controller/database.env, which must be root-owned with mode 0600.
.SH FILES
/usr/share/doc/supivpn-controller/examples/controller.example.json
.br
/usr/share/doc/supivpn-controller/DEBIAN_PACKAGING.md.gz
.br
/usr/share/doc/supivpn-controller/POSTGRES.md.gz
